      "problem": "If $‖2x‖=1$, find $‖-14x‖.$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kx‖=|k|\\cdot ‖x‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2x‖ & =1 \\\\ |2|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =1 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $‖-14x‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-14x‖ & =14\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =14\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
